# NOTE on SauceScript (`*.sauce.ts`, `sdk/src/std`, `dev-tools/sauce`): it IS formatted. It is
# ordinary TypeScript syntax, so prettier handles it — the stdlib's TS-annotated `.js` only needed
# its parser named, which `.prettierrc.json`'s `overrides` does. ESLint is the one that excludes
# these, for reasons that do not apply to a formatter: `main` is the entry point the Sauce compiler
# calls (so `no-unused-vars` fires on every program) and `require(cond)` is SauceScript's ASSERTION,
# which `no-require-imports` reads as a module import.

# GENERATED sources. `ci.yml` asserts `sdk/src/deployments` still matches a fresh
# `sync-engine-artifacts` run, and the generators emit their own (unformatted) text — so
# formatting the committed copy diverges it from what regeneration produces and fails that check.
# The generator is the thing to change, not its output.
**/*.generated.ts

